WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.090
There’s no doubt that the SCP Foundation
has come across some dangerous anomalies over

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.200
the years.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.400
If you had to guess, what would you say is
the most dangerous SCP they have in containment?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:18.430
A lot of people might immediately think of
SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile, and

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.659
perhaps they’d might be right.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:25.189
After all, we’re talking about a gigantic
lizard that can regenerate almost all forms

00:00:25.189 --> 00:00:30.859
of damage, and harbors a burning hatred for
any and all other forms of life.

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:35.880
Then there’s the various eldritch entities
the Foundation has come into contact with,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.440
beings that could easily rewrite all of reality
out of pure anger, or just to torment us for

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.160
their own amusement.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:48.839
But the most dangerous SCP might well be something
completely unassuming.

00:00:48.839 --> 00:00:53.389
Instead of a zombie producing plague doctor,
or an actual plague of flesh eating zombies

00:00:53.389 --> 00:00:57.230
, imagine if there was just a man.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:01:03.590
One seemingly ordinary human man, nothing
about him that looks unusual, no memetic or

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:04.840
anomalous superpower.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:10.730
And yet, one look at him tells you he’s
the most dangerous man you’ve ever seen,

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:15.910
someone who should be locked up forever for
all the horrible things he’s done.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:24.080
Welcome to the story of Fraisure Melbrook,
the Most Dangerous Person, also known as SCP-3017.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.080
To anyone that knew him, Fraisure was just
an ordinary man.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.450
Although, at twenty five years of age, he
had not exactly lived a charmed life.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:37.840
People would look at him and could almost
tell there was something unsavory about Fraisure’s

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.840
character.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:42.350
It was as if one glance could somehow tell
you that he was trouble.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:47.760
It was this unshakable feeling that he gave
people that led to Fraisure Melbrook being

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.760
arrested.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.050
And arrested.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.080
And arrested some more.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.200
Over the course of his adult life, he was
placed under arrest a total of twenty-three

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.470
times.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:02.410
Fraisure was suspected to have committed a
number of different crimes, ranging from robbery

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.930
and assault, all the way up to accusations
of murder.

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:10.550
Interestingly, he was never formally indicted
for any of his alleged crimes, meaning he

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:13.700
was only ever arrested and held as a suspect.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.050
But never once was he confirmed to have been
guilty.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:22.580
There was never any evidence, nothing to prove
beyond reasonable doubt that Fraisure was,

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:24.370
in fact, a criminal.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:29.260
Instead, every arrest boiled down to the way
he made people in his presence feel.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.750
Unfortunately, even though he was never proven
to be guilty, or even capable of committing

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:39.960
the crimes he was accused of, Fraisure Melbrook’s
multiple arrests garnered him a notable criminal

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:43.900
record, and soon drew the attention of the
SCP Foundation.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:50.740
When he was transferred into Foundation containment
and designated as SCP-3017, it was believed

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.560
that Fraisure had some form of connection
to a number of Groups of Interest.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:00.760
These are various organizations that the Foundation
monitors, viewing them as causes for concern

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:03.420
and sometimes outright threats.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.160
This list includes The Church of The Broken
God; a cult of religious zealots that worship

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.830
an entity that combines a number of SCPs.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:16.860
As well as the Global Occult Coalition, a
gung-ho organization policing the paranormal

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.960
that shares an uneasy history with the Foundation.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:24.590
However, no member of staff could explain
exactly why they thought Fraisure Melbrook

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:30.709
had any connection to these groups, there
was no evidence that he was, but still, they

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.930
had a hunch.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.140
And so, testing began.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.720
Hours upon hours of rigorous interviews and
experimentation, trying to understand what

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:44.060
it was that made people want to keep this
seemingly ordinary man locked up.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:48.580
After extensive research was conducted by
Foundation personnel, they were able to determine

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:54.989
why SCP-3017 had been arrested so many times
before, and what had drawn the Foundation

00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:57.599
to him in the first place.

00:03:57.599 --> 00:04:01.080
Fraisure Melbrook was suffering from a cognitohazard.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:05.500
This was a condition that did not so much
have a direct, adverse effect on him, but

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.480
rather influenced those around him.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.470
Anyone that stood close enough to SCP-3017,
or made an attempt to engage him directly

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:19.289
in conversation, even those that just looked
at him, all reacted the same way.

00:04:19.289 --> 00:04:24.321
Fraisure gave people the overwhelming belief
that he needed to be placed in custody, even

00:04:24.321 --> 00:04:29.180
if he’d not said or done anything to give
them a reason to.

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:35.969
Anyone that looked at, spoke to, or even stood
near him became spontaneously aware that SCP-3017

00:04:35.969 --> 00:04:38.270
was some sort of dangerous criminal.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:43.290
The cognitohazard didn’t give people knowledge
of his exact crimes, it more just made them

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.630
believe that Fraisure had a violent disposition
and that he needed to be locked away.

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:54.419
Any person staying within the vicinity of
SCP-3017 for an hour or longer would experience

00:04:54.419 --> 00:04:57.789
further effects of Fraisure’s cognitohazard.

00:04:57.789 --> 00:05:02.749
Beyond just knowing there was something untowards
about him, those who spent extended time around

00:05:02.749 --> 00:05:08.830
SCP-3017 would actively try to restrain him,
and then after an hour they would exhibit

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.029
violent behavior towards him.

00:05:11.029 --> 00:05:15.990
They would start obsessively trying to ensure
he was incarcerated, almost like the thought

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:21.530
of him being free was so horrifying that they
couldn’t help but try to arrest him themselves.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:26.520
Luckily, these effects of longer exposure
to Fraisure were not permanent and often the

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.690
subjects’ tendencies to try and restrain
him could be cured through amnestics.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:35.240
The effects of Fraisure Melbrook’s cognitohazardous
condition seemed to change relative to the

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:38.219
amount of time he remained incarcerated.

00:05:38.219 --> 00:05:43.729
After continuous exposure to SCP-3017, the
effects of his cognitohazard would appear

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:48.590
to fade, meaning that those who had previously
been compelled to incarcerate him would later

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:52.509
become indifferent, or even release him freely.

00:05:52.509 --> 00:05:57.360
This caused a problem for the Foundation and
raised a very important question: How do you

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.580
contain someone that you later feel the urge
to set free?

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:07.900
The answer was designated SCP-3017-1, a list
of individuals with a connection to Fraisure

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:13.580
Melbrook, all of whom had seemingly become
immune to the outward effects of his condition.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.460
Not one of these people could be convinced
that Fraisure was the violent criminal that

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.909
everyone else saw.

00:06:18.909 --> 00:06:23.900
Among the list of names were Frasure’s parents
Vivian and Beck, along with his siblings,

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:29.289
grandmother, former classmates, and romantic
partners, and his fiancé Nadia.

00:06:29.289 --> 00:06:34.210
But, you might be wondering, how did the SCP
Foundation use nothing more than a list of

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:37.719
names to keep SCP-3017 caged?

00:06:37.719 --> 00:06:40.530
By threatening them, of course.

00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:44.119
Researchers who interviewed Fraisure found
that they could greatly decrease the secondary

00:06:44.119 --> 00:06:48.360
effect of his condition, making them far less
compelled to free him.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.949
All it took was for them to tell Fraisure
that his family, friends, fiancé would be

00:06:52.949 --> 00:06:57.560
captured, tortured, or even killed if he tried
to escape containment.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.539
According to the Foundation, this didn’t
stop Fraisure from trying to escape though.

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:07.379
His file states that he actively made several
attempts to breach containment, all of which

00:07:07.379 --> 00:07:08.379
failed.

00:07:08.379 --> 00:07:12.430
The truth, however, was that just about any
move that Fraisure made was misinterpreted

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.249
as an attempted escape.

00:07:14.249 --> 00:07:20.119
In one instance, while just trying to use
the bathroom, SCP-3017 was tackled and restrained

00:07:20.119 --> 00:07:21.699
by a Foundation guard.

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:26.219
You see, Fraisure knew that just like with
his previous arrests, he’d done nothing

00:07:26.219 --> 00:07:30.300
to deserve being locked up and interrogated
by the SCP Foundation.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:34.919
But, to the eyes of everyone around him, he
was a dangerous threat.

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:39.811
The researchers and guards treated him like
a monster, because as far as they saw, he

00:07:39.811 --> 00:07:40.870
was one.

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:44.939
By manipulating information about the current
health of his loved ones, like telling him

00:07:44.939 --> 00:07:49.740
his grandmother had developed lung cancer,
the Foundation kept Fraisure under lock and

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.740
key.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:55.160
Hearing threats against his friends and family,
or bad news about their current state quickly

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:59.159
put an end to SCP-3017’s attempts at escape.

00:07:59.159 --> 00:08:04.059
Even though he was frustrated with the Foundation,
he was without hope, and had little choice

00:08:04.059 --> 00:08:05.089
in the matter.

00:08:05.089 --> 00:08:10.270
So, Fraisure did his best to comply with his
captors and offer the SCP Foundation information

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:14.990
on Groups of Interest he thought they wanted
to hear, even though he had no affiliation

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.529
with any of them.

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:21.969
By bringing Fraisure’s fiancé, Nadia, into
containment and showing him a live video feed

00:08:21.969 --> 00:08:27.300
of her, Foundation researcher Doctor Kiran
hoped to coax a wealth of valuable information

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:30.029
out of SCP-3017.

00:08:30.029 --> 00:08:34.500
Afraid for his partner’s life, Fraisure
did his best to answer their questions, and

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.130
Nadia was later freed and given amnestics
to forget the incident.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:42.779
But Foundation Researcher Rylan was quick
to realize that the information Doctor Kiran

00:08:42.779 --> 00:08:47.140
had extracted from SCP-3017 didn’t seem
to add up.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:51.680
Fraisure, of course, had no knowledge about
any Groups of Interest, and had to improvise

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:53.920
to protect his fiancé.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:58.810
Researcher Rylan picked up on this, remarking
that SCP-3017’s information could not be

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:04.620
considered reliable, but she was unsure if
Fraisure was hiding something or simply didn’t

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.110
know anything.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:10.310
During another interrogation, Fraisure’s
brother, a former classmate and two former

00:09:10.310 --> 00:09:13.550
romantic partners were brought into the Foundation
and sedated.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:19.150
In an adjacent room, Fraisure was threatened
by Doctor Kiran with a handgun and made to

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.810
answer further questions.

00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:25.180
Every time he didn’t, the doctor threatened
to shoot one of Fraisure’s loved ones.

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:29.600
It was after this incident that Researcher
Rylan once again reassessed the information

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:31.500
given by SCP-3017.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:36.870
Finally, she came to realize that there was
no evidence of Fraisure’s criminal history,

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:40.310
nor was there anything tying him to Groups
of Interest.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:45.110
Everything that the Foundation had thought
of him was just a result of SCP-3017’s condition,

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:50.089
and he genuinely had none of the information
they’d been seeking.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:55.040
He was only answering their questions to protect
the lives of people he cared for.

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:59.690
Realizing the huge ethical mistake the Foundation
had made, essentially psychologically torturing

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:04.980
Fraisure for information he simply didn’t
have, Researcher Rylan begged her superiors

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:07.970
that SCP-3017 be released.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:13.000
The request was denied, and instead Rylan
was contained, believed to be a new instance

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.080
of SCP-3017-1.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:21.170
With the help of Security Officer Rudolf Caridad,
who had guarded Fraisure, Rylan escaped her

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:24.800
own cell and the pair of them triggered a
containment alarm.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:30.970
In the ensuing confusion, Rylan and Caridad
freed SCP-3017 from his incarceration, and

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:35.780
she and Fraisure escaped the containment facility
while Officer Caridad was captured and contained

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:37.560
by security personnel.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:41.430
Rylan brought Fraisure to what she thought
was the safety of his family home.

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:44.370
But neither of them expected to see what awaited
them.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:49.819
The house had been burned to the ground, with
almost all of Frasiure’s family inside.

00:10:49.819 --> 00:10:56.290
His parents, siblings, grandmother, fiancé
and even neighbor had all perished in a fire

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:00.310
that had engulfed the one place in the world
that Fraisure hadn’t been held against his

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.310
will.

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:05.490
It is still unclear if the fire was intentionally
started by a member of the SCP Foundation

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:11.550
to drive SCP-3017 back to containment or had
merely been an unfortunate accident.

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:18.050
But notably, Doctor Kiran had been strangely
absent during SCP-3017 and Rylan’s escape

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.190
from the Foundation.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:24.839
Overwhelmed with grief and despair, Fraisure
was last seen on a bridge not far from his

00:11:24.839 --> 00:11:30.579
childhood home, and Researcher Rylan was recaptured
without resistance by Foundation personnel

00:11:30.579 --> 00:11:32.610
near the same spot.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:39.420
With SCP-3017 gone along with his cognitohazardous
effects, both her and Security Officer Caridad

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.880
were reinstated back to full employment with
the Foundation.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:48.009
The Foundation then reclassified SCP-3017
as ‘neutralized’, quietly avoiding the

00:11:48.009 --> 00:11:52.029
truth of their mistake
All records of his supposed criminal activity

00:11:52.029 --> 00:11:56.699
and links to anomalous groups were stricken
from the record as unsubstantiated.

00:11:56.699 --> 00:12:01.889
He had been innocent all along, just a man
who had never done anything he was accused

00:12:01.889 --> 00:12:04.790
of and didn’t deserve to be locked away.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:09.480
The SCP Foundation had tortured Fraisure,
asking him questions he didn’t have the

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:15.250
answers to, using the love he had for those
closest to him as a way to try and goad him

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:20.290
into giving the Foundation what they wanted,
and in the end, may have been responsible

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:23.550
for multiple innocent people being murdered.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:28.480
Perhaps it was easier for them to stamp ‘neutralized’
on his file than to actually face up to what

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:29.959
they’d done to him.

00:12:29.959 --> 00:12:34.570
The Foundation has spent at least a century
containing anomalies and monsters, but the

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:39.629
hardest monsters to contain are often the
ones that emerge within us.

00:12:39.629 --> 00:12:46.830
And nothing better illustrates that than the
Foundation’s monstrous treatment of SCP-3017.

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:53.360
Now check out “SCP-5094 - Miss J's Whiz
Kidz Schoolhouse” and “SCP-507 - Reluctant

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:58.739
Dimension Hopper” for more SCP Foundation
stories that’ll tug at your heartstrings!

